  "starterCode": "# Gemma 3 Attention Block — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(q, k, v, gate=None):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Gemma 3 Attention Block** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(q, k, v, gate=None):\n    q=np.asarray(q,dtype=float); k=np.asarray(k,dtype=float); v=np.asarray(v,dtype=float)\n    scores=q@np.swapaxes(k,-1,-2)/np.sqrt(q.shape[-1])\n    e=np.exp(scores-scores.max(axis=-1,keepdims=True)); p=e/e.sum(axis=-1,keepdims=True)\n    out=p@v\n    if gate is not None: out=out/(1+np.exp(-np.asarray(gate,dtype=float)))\n    return out.tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
